 subgraph RECOVERY[" "]
    direction TB
        RECOVERY_H["IF THEY STALL OR GO DARK AT ANY POINT"]:::sgHeader
        REC1["STALLED (still engaging but not advancing)<br>THE SYSTEM NOW DIAGNOSES WHY (v1.9):<br>- Opens emails but never clicks = wrong story angle (system switches to different story)<br>- Clicks emails but never books = trust gap (system injects authority proof + guarantee)<br>- Watches video but no action = urgency gap (system fires sprint burst with deadline)<br>- Books then cancels = commitment anxiety (system sends what-to-expect reassurance)<br>- Was engaged then went silent = distraction (system switches channel, fires pattern interrupt)<br>Each of these triggers a DIFFERENT automated response. Not more of the same.<br>Flash Sale urgency sequence (5 messages)<br>If no response: Downsell (lower commitment option)<br>If no response: Seinfeld weekly broadcast (90 days of stories)<br>  Rotating: SA1 to SA3 to SA2 to SA5 to SA4 across 12 weeks<br>If score spikes: re-enter booking automatically<br>MOMENTUM LAYER: If prospect clicks booking link at ANY point during stall recovery, skip ahead"]
        REC2["GONE DARK - 5 RECOVERY PATHS BASED ON WHAT HAPPENED IN LP<br>ALL COUNTS: unique prospects (first-touch 2021+, deduplicated)<br>CRITICAL: TIME-LAPSE MESSAGING applies to ALL recovery paths<br>Under 90 days since last contact: warm continuity - reference prior interaction naturally<br>91-365 days: cool re-relevance - DO NOT claim active relationship, lead with problem relevance<br>Over 365 days: cold pattern interrupt - treat as new lead with data, no prior contact reference<br>  Example: DO NOT say when we stopped by your home 2 years later<br>  Instead: Homeowners in [their city] are discovering something about their windows<br>GHL reads the Lead Perfection disposition code to route correctly:<br>PATH 1 - DEAD LEADS: DNC / NoHome / Bad Lead (2,156 prospects)<br>  No outreach. Suppress from all GHL sequences.<br>PATH 2 - STALE APPOINTMENT (Set/Confirmed in LP, 2,900 prospects, 378 days avg):<br>  Single SMS check-in only: Are you still in the market?<br>  If yes - rep task. If no reply after 7 days - long-term nurture.<br>  Do NOT send booking links (appointment already exists in LP)<br>PATH 3 - APPOINTMENT CANCELLED BEFORE DEMO (CXL + NS + No Demo, 7,484 prospects):<br>  CXL = the appointment was CANCELLED before the demo ran<br>  These leads BOOKED ONCE. They had enough trust. Remove friction and rebook.<br>  Rebook rescue sequence (4 messages) - soft, no guilt, easy re-schedule<br>  Do NOT restart indoctrination from scratch<br>PATH 4 - DEMO HAPPENED, NO SALE (5,513 prospects):<br>  OPPFDN: objection handling sequence (default price/timing branch if no tag)<br>    Default branch: Price/Timing (most common at $48K job size)<br>  1Leg (One Spouse Present, 231 leads, avg 3 years old): objection:spouse sequence<br>    Message MUST acknowledge time has passed: We met a while back - are both of you ready now?<br>PATH 5 - NEVER REACHED DEMO (21,823 prospects):<br>  SPRINT REACTIVATION (v1.8 - campaign bursts, NOT slow drips)<br>  Stale leads do not respond to consistency. They respond to DISRUPTION.<br>  4 SPRINT BURSTS over 84 days with SILENCE between each:<br>  Sprint 1 (Days 1-5): Code compliance angle - 3 emails + 1 SMS then go silent 21 days<br>  Sprint 2 (Days 26-30): Social proof angle - 2 emails + 1 SMS then go silent 25 days<br>  Sprint 3 (Days 55-59): Scarcity angle - limited slots + deadline then go silent 21 days<br>  Sprint 4 (Days 80-84): Final push + file close<br>  Each sprint has a STRONG ANGLE + STRONG OFFER + HARD DEADLINE<br>  Between sprints: SILENCE (no drip, no nurture, nothing)<br>  If the system detects a momentum spike during silence: capture immediately<br>  Every message includes a direct booking link"]
  end

